\text{hypotenuse} = \sqrt{7^2 + 7^2} = \sqrt{49 + 49} = \sqrt{98} = 7\sqrt{2}
\] Therefore, the perimeter of one of these triangles is: \[
7 + 7 + 7\sqrt{2} = 14 + 7\sqrt{2}
\] The final answer is: \[
